# Breakfast of Champions — Meta Workspace

Two-repo workspace. Treat paths carefully.

## Layout

- `specs/` — design source of truth
  - `specs/canonical/` — accepted system behavior
    - `game_loop.md` — Run vs Combat architecture
    - `characters.md` — Breakfast Foods & Enemies
    - `map_system.md` — multi-path map / node logic
  - `specs/active_deltas/` — in-flight design deltas (pre-merge)
- `openspec/` — OpenSpec change workflow tooling
  - `openspec/changes/` — proposals, formal deltas, archive
  - `openspec/specs/` — optional formal OpenSpec mirrors (keep in sync with `specs/canonical/` when used)
- `game-project/` — Godot game implementation (separate git repo)
  - `scenes/`, `scripts/`, `project.godot`

Open this folder (`breakfast-of-champions-meta/`) as the Cursor workspace root.

## OpenSpec workflow (Cursor)

Use slash commands (restart Cursor if they are missing):

- `/opsx-explore` — think through an idea before committing
- `/opsx-propose` — draft proposal, specs, design, and tasks
- `/opsx-apply` — implement the change from its task list
- `/opsx-sync` — merge delta specs into main specs
- `/opsx-archive` — finish a change and archive it
- `/opsx-update` — revise planning artifacts

CLI checks: `openspec list`, `openspec show <change>`, `openspec validate <change>`.

## Spec-first rules

1. Specs under `specs/canonical/` are authoritative. Read them before implementing.
2. Prefer an active delta (`specs/active_deltas/` or `openspec/changes/`) over inventing behavior that contradicts canonical specs.
3. Keep intent and acceptance criteria in specs; keep implementation in `game-project/`.

## Godot implementation rules

1. Put scenes in `game-project/scenes/` and scripts in `game-project/scripts/`.
2. Prefer small, named scripts over large god-objects.
3. Respect `game-project/.gitignore` (never commit `.godot/`).
4. Meta-repo commits must not swallow the nested Godot repo.

## Git boundaries

- Meta repo: tracks OpenSpec, Cursor config, and meta tooling.
- Godot repo (`game-project/`): tracks game assets and `project.godot`.
- Never mix commits across the two remotes in one operation.
